<title>PORTUGAL: POLL - Portugal spreads vs Bunds, Spanish Bonos.</title>
<headline>POLL - Portugal spreads vs Bunds, Spanish Bonos.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the daily forecast for spreads in the Portuguese bond market based on a poll of four banks and one brokerage.</p>
<p>Poll covers spreads between the February 2007 Portuguese cash bond (OT) and the German and Spanish equivalents, together with the spreads between the Portuguese 10 and two-year bonds.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>			     Min spread Avge  Max  vs previous close</p>
<p>Feb 07 vs Bund July  07   70 bps   71    72	    72</p>
<p>Feb 07 vs Bono March 07     6	6.6    7	     7</p>
<p>						  YLDS3</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>				 Min  Avge   Max</p>
<p>Feb 07 vs March 99	 108  109.2  110     vs     110</p>
<p>						  PT/CURVE</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Key factors likely to affect market:</p>
<p>- The 10 year bonds were seen gaining with Europe but the spread with the Bund would narrowly only slightly. The market will be well-supported along the curve but the strength of the longer end will prevent any steepening, traders said.</p>
<p>--Sergio Goncalves, Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
